    "_about": "THE WILD BOAR (2026-11-05, 2nd pass: the belly up on longer legs, a grizzled coat -- grey-brown with a darker back, a paler cheek, a dark snout and legs, bristle sheen -- a deeper shorter wedge of a head, an upright brush of a crest): high heavy shoulders and a back falling to narrow hindquarters, the body pressed flat from the sides under its bark-grizzled coat, a crest of long bristles along the spine highest over the withers; a long wedge of a head out to the snout disc, small erect tufted ears, the kept tusks curling up from the lip flanges; slimmer longer legs on small dark trotters; the tail kept (2026-11-08) The TUSKS are a sharp `horn` (pointed, keeled, twisting up and out) and the EARS `fin` sheets (cupped, a dark tip, the base buried in an earBase fillet): sharp.js.",
